{"title":"quietly public interview with carolyn yoo","link":"https://keningzhu.com/journal/interview-quietly-public","date":1784189909000,"content":" \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/f43bc894-75ca-481a-96d8-7ecf1d55ad22/quietly+public+interview.gif?format=1000w\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1069\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/f43bc894-75ca-481a-96d8-7ecf1d55ad22/quietly+public+interview.gif?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/f43bc894-75ca-481a-96d8-7ecf1d55ad22/quietly+public+interview.gif?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/f43bc894-75ca-481a-96d8-7ecf1d55ad22/quietly+public+interview.gif?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/f43bc894-75ca-481a-96d8-7ecf1d55ad22/quietly+public+interview.gif?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/f43bc894-75ca-481a-96d8-7ecf1d55ad22/quietly+public+interview.gif?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/f43bc894-75ca-481a-96d8-7ecf1d55ad22/quietly+public+interview.gif?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/f43bc894-75ca-481a-96d8-7ecf1d55ad22/quietly+public+interview.gif?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n  <hr />\n  \n    \n\n    \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n  <p>earlier this spring I did an <a href=\"https://cyoo.substack.com/p/building-a-world-not-an-audience\" target=\"_blank\">interview</a> about going <a href=\"https://cyoo.substack.com/p/quietly-public-on-the-internet\" target=\"_blank\">Quietly Public</a> with Carolyn Yoo for her newsletter, <a href=\"https://cyoo.substack.com/\" target=\"_blank\">SEE YOU</a>. I talk about sharing work outside of validation, how I came to grow worlds, the veil between private &amp; public, and how the internet is just a room you can choose to be alone in. </p><p>I love exploring <a href=\"https://garden.carolynyoo.com/\">Carolyn’s digital garden</a> and her post on how to <a href=\"https://cyoo.substack.com/p/intro-to-digital-gardening-a-quietly\" target=\"_blank\">make your own digital garden</a> — as well as by her <a href=\"https://cyoo.substack.com/t/zines\">zine-making</a> practices, reading her deeply nuanced introspections, and her resources, collections, and systems for the creative life. Carolyn is an immediate kindred spirit internet friend who I also had the pleasure to share space with in season 2 of <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/labyrinth\">Labyrinth</a>, as well as meeting and wandering through (actual!) parks and labyrinths in real life. <br /><br /><a href=\"https://cyoo.substack.com/p/building-a-world-not-an-audience\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>read the interview</strong></a></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n  <hr />\n  \n    \n\n    \n\n\n\n  \n\n ","author":"Kening Zhu","siteTitle":"kening zhu","siteHash":"ef8a94b9fc20c32a4ee7d94ee971337d278e8b2fafe747123e4eb5cea026e84e","entryHash":"8c383e1940c78df22ef016855a0fb3f308798a37762e3193554033555a6b1228","category":"Sites"}